o fifteen thousand dollars towards  his student loans just to return it's a  deal Kaela parson ski couldn't pass up  her ten thousand dollar scholarship paid  for undergraduate loans which helped her  buy her first house there's a great  opportunity to financially it took a big  load off of me and I think it's worth it  can you see yourself here for a long  time yeah I couldn't lessee myself here  for a long time st. Clair County a  picturesque collection of small towns  and cities runs along Lake Huron and the  Saint Clair River a quiet county with  plenty of small-town appeal the average  annual salary here is just under 52  thousand dollars slightly more than the  national average why are you having to  pay people to come here I know it seems  ironic to think that Randy Myers helped  create the come home award let us focus  on talent and works with local  businesses and organizations to help  fund it to reverse a brain drain from  the area I think a part of it is that  the young people that grow up here they  get a chance to leave after high school  and go to college and they want to get  away from small-town America I mean you  know I can't play them the lure of  Detroit or Chicago nearby or the  Carolinas it draws people away less than  eighteen percent of st. Claire's a  hundred and sixty thousand residents  have a college degree  compare that with nearby Washtenaw  County home to University of Michigan  where more than half have a college  degree it's not a jobs problem this is  worth it this LinkedIn editor-at-large  chip cutter says the issue is educated  and trained workers so we're seeing this  real trend across the u.s. where places  like New York or San Francisco or Boston  these cities that just keep attracting  the type of educated workers that  employers crave it's kind of a rich get  richer situation it's why incentive  programs are popping up around counties  towns and small cities across America  like Crawford County Ohio Grant County  Indiana and